 "text": "Hi, how are you doing right now? Want to get lower or find a nearby shelter? Thunder usually means there's rain coming too. That's reasonable. A good rock overhang is very safe during a storm. Sure thing. Nod and I'll light the candles. Put it together as best you can before you leave. Pop up tents hate being packed while they' still fully inflated. Try to get as high up as possible and stay dry. Then wait for the storm to pass. If you' caught outside for several hours, a simple tarp gives quite a lot of protection. Then head for the hill and the shelter. Pick a spot out of the wind and get inside as quickly as you can.",
